Spec: ServiceMaintenanceWindows

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  The two maintenance-window hook pass-throughs, `./maintenance_start.rhai` and
    `./maintenance_stop.rhai`, frozen as ONE spec: two 5-line stubs of identical shape
    (grouping justification: same-basename convention would duplicate byte-equivalent
    contract text four times — these two files plus their byte-identical tenant twins
    verified by diff), each exposing only a `run` that brackets pre/post hooks while the
    actual scaling stays an unimplemented TODO.

Owns:
  ./maintenance_start.rhai
  ./maintenance_stop.rhai

Exposes:
  @run(context) — identical @fn name in both files; reached by the backup/restore and
    init lanes as `import_run("maintenance_start"/"maintenance_stop", context)` sites
    frozen in ./backup.sdd, ./restore.sdd (and ./init_from.sdd by contrast: NO call
    there — restore-only pairing).

Accepts:
  @context — the service build-context map; the stubs READ NOTHING from it (the lists
    named in the TODO comments, deployment_list/statefulset_list/scale_target, are never
    touched) and mutate nothing.

Returns:
  Unit in both lanes: no `return`, hook @import_run results are INVOKED FOR EFFECT ONLY
    and never merged back (contrast the bucket `type_of == "map"` merge discipline in
    ./install.sdd) — a shadowed hook returning a new map is silently dropped.

Raises:
  Zero @throw sites. Failure lanes: a hook module whose FILE exists but whose
    `maintenance_start_pre`/`_post` (resp. stop) `run` raises propagates out of
    @import_run (wynil-core skips only absent-module/absent-run per
    ./../service/context.sdd shim freeze) and the surrounding backup/restore try/catch
    turns it into a FAILED throw + exit 4/5. An absent hook file skips silently.
  Engine property errors are impossible here: no property access at all.

Must:
  Keep the TODO comments as the ONLY record of intent: start scales "scalables" to 0,
    stop scales to `context.scale_target` — NEITHER is implemented today, so every
    caller's "maintenance window" (backup.sdd, restore.sdd) currently brackets
    NOTHING; frozen, not fixed.
  Import-run EXACTLY the four hook names `maintenance_start_pre`,
    `maintenance_start_post`, `maintenance_stop_pre`, `maintenance_stop_post` —
    shipped by nobody in-repo (package-slot convention only).
  Leave hook calls OUTSIDE any try/catch (frozen: raises escape; the callers, not these
    stubs, own marking).
  Stay byte-identical with ./../tenant/maintenance_{start,stop}.rhai (diff-verified);
    tenant call sites (./../tenant/backup.sdd, ./../tenant/restore.sdd pending) share
    this contract verbatim.

Depends on:
  ./context.sdd — wynil-core @import_run skip/raise shim.
  ./backup.sdd, ./restore.sdd — the only callers (window brackets both lanes; restore
    brackets the whole engine ladder, and NEITHER scales anything while these are TODO).

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide later the real scale-to-0/scale-target implementation (which workloads
      are even trackable here: the lists come from backup_context env-encoded names,
      and init_from.sdd shows the Job lane waiting 20 min) — until then the spec
      freezes a no-op window and every "maintenance protects the restore" assumption
      made elsewhere is FICTION; keep this cross-referenced in any backup-lane review.
  [ ] Decide whether hook returns should merge like buckets (currently discarded).
  [ ] Add mock tests: no test in agent/tests exercises these two files (their hook
      slots never ship), scenarios unmapped.

Done when:
  Either the TODO scaling lands (spec then regrows Must clauses) or the windows are
    retired; tests cover hook-raise escape and silent-skip posture either way.

Scenario: window opens and closes doing nothing
  Given `ServiceMaintenanceWindows` with no maintenance_* hook files in any resolver
    dir
  When a backup lane import_runs start then stop
  Then both return unit, skip all four hooks silently, and no workload changes —
    the backup runs against live, unscaled deployments
